---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SearchBox from '../../components/SearchBox.astro';
import seeds from '../../data/seeds.json';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: [
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'What is a Minecraft seed?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'A seed is a number (or text, which the game converts to a number) that determines the entire world generation: terrain, biomes, structures and ore placement. Two players using the same seed and game version get the same world.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Do seeds work on both Java and Bedrock?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Since the 1.18 update, the same numeric seed generates the same terrain and biomes on Java and Bedrock. Structure placement (villages, temples, strongholds) still differs between editions.' } },
    { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How do I see the seed of my world?',
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Type /seed in chat (needs cheats or operator). On a server you do not own, the seed is hidden from regular players.' } }
  ]
};
---
<Base title="Minecraft Seeds" description="Minecraft seeds explained: how they work, Java vs Bedrock differences, and famous verified seeds like pack.png and the title screen panoramas." canonicalPath="/seeds/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="container">
    <nav class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Seeds</nav>
    <h1>Minecraft Seeds</h1>
    <p class="sub">How seeds work, plus famous seeds documented and verified by the community.</p>
    <SearchBox placeholder="Search seeds, biomes, structures..." />

    <h2>How seeds work</h2>
    <p>A seed is the number Minecraft uses to generate a world: terrain, biomes, structures and ore veins all come from it. Enter the same seed in the same game version and you get the same world. Text seeds ("glacier", your name...) are converted to numbers behind the scenes.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Java vs Bedrock:</strong> since 1.18, the same numeric seed produces the same terrain and biome layout in both editions. Structures (villages, temples, strongholds) still generate in different spots per edition.</li>
      <li><strong>Find your seed:</strong> type <code>/seed</code> in chat (cheats or server operator required).</li>
      <li><strong>Version matters:</strong> world generation changes between major versions, so a seed from 1.16 generates a different world in 1.21. Always match the seed to its documented version.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Famous seeds</h2>
    <div class="grid-cards">
      {seeds.map(s => (
        <a class="card" href={`/seeds/${s.slug}/`}>
          <div class="icon"><Icon name="sprout" /></div>
          <h3>{s.name}</h3>
          <p>Seed: {s.seed}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p class="notice-fan" style="margin-top:16px">We only list seeds documented and verified by the community, with sources. Seed hunting for your own style of world (spawn village, cherry ring, trial chambers nearby) is version-specific - a curated, verified list is in progress.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
